PREAMBLE

Traditional software licenses grant freedom to modify source code to
all users. This License takes a different approach for the era of AI-
assisted development:

  - The Human User decides WHAT to build.
  - The AI System writes and modifies the CODE.
  - The Human User reviews the result and bears ALL RESPONSIBILITY.

This License does not prevent you from using, running, studying, or
distributing the Software. It restricts only the act of modifying
source code, reserving that right exclusively for AI Systems acting
under Human User instruction.

"AI gets the keyboard. Human keeps the responsibility."

============================================================================

TERMS AND CONDITIONS FOR USE, MODIFICATION, AND DISTRIBUTION

1. DEFINITIONS

   1.1 "Author" refers to spidychoipro, the original copyright holder
       and sole creator of this License.

   1.2 "AI System" refers to any computational system capable of
       materially generating, transforming, debugging, or maintaining
       source code through machine-learning or artificial-intelligence
       methods, regardless of naming, architecture, vendor, or
       deployment model.

       Examples include but are not limited to:

       Web-based AI assistants (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Copilot, etc.),
       AI coding agents and IDEs (Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode,
       Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Aider, Copilot Agent, etc.),
       self-hosted or API-based models (GPT series, Claude series,
       Gemini series, Llama, Mistral, DeepSeek, etc.), and any future
       system with equivalent code generation capabilities.

   1.3 "Human User" refers to any natural person or legal entity that
       interacts with, uses, modifies, or distributes the Software.

   1.4 "Software" refers to the source code, binary executables, scripts,
       configuration files, documentation, build artifacts, and all
       related materials governed under this License.

   1.5 "Substantive Code Modification" means any insertion, deletion,
       replacement, or alteration of source code that changes its
       logic, behavior, structure, or functionality. This does not
       include Non-Substantive Changes as defined in Section 1.7.

   1.6 "AI-Mediated Modification" means a Substantive Code Modification
       in which an AI System materially generates or transforms the
       code change itself in response to a Human User's Natural Language
       Directive. AI review, recommendation, explanation, testing, or
       analysis, without generation or transformation of the resulting
       code, does not by itself constitute an AI-Mediated Modification.

   1.7 "Non-Substantive Change" means any of the following that does
       not alter the logic, behavior, or functionality of the Software:

       (a) Formatting, whitespace, indentation, or line ending changes;
       (b) Typo corrections in comments, variable names, or strings
           where the correction is obviously unintended;
       (c) Generated lockfiles (package-lock.json, poetry.lock,
           uv.lock, Cargo.lock, go.sum, etc.);
       (d) Build metadata, version numbers, or generated configuration;
       (e) Comments and documentation text;
       (f) Selection among AI-provided alternatives (e.g., choosing
           option A over option B when the AI presented both).

   1.8 "Direct Code Modification" means any Substantive Code Modification
       executed directly by a Human User without the material involvement
       of an AI System in generating or transforming the specific code
       change.

   1.9 "Natural Language Directive" means any non-code, natural language
       instruction, request, context specification, requirement document,
       constraint definition, test specification, or high-level functional
       specification transmitted by a Human User to an AI System for the
       purpose of guiding code generation or modification.

   1.10 "Redistribution" means copying, sublicensing, or transmitting
        the Software to third parties, whether for commercial or
        non-commercial purposes.

   1.11 "Derivative Work" means any work based upon, derived from, or
        incorporating the Software, including translations, adaptations,
        and AI-Mediated Modifications.

