       royalty-free, irrevocable license to:

       (a) Use, run, execute, and interact with the Software for any
           purpose, commercial or non-commercial;
       (b) Study, inspect, analyze, and reverse-engineer the Software
           source code for educational, research, or verification
           purposes;
       (c) Create and distribute unmodified copies of the Software;
       (d) Create and distribute AI-Mediated Modifications of the
           Software, provided such modifications comply with Section 3;
       (e) Sublicense the rights granted under this Section to third
           parties, provided all recipients are bound by this License.

   2.2 Modification Right. The right to create Substantive Code
       Modifications of the Software may be exercised only through
       an AI System. A Human User may formulate Natural Language
       Directives, specifications, constraints, and tests, but may
       not directly alter the substantive source code.

   2.3 All rights not expressly granted under this License are reserved
       by the Author.

3. WORKFLOW: AI-MEDIATED MODIFICATION

   3.1 The intended workflow for modifying the Software is as follows:

       Step 1: The Human User formulates a Natural Language Directive
       describing what change is needed and why.

       Step 2: The AI System receives the directive and generates or
       transforms the source code accordingly.

       Step 3: The Human User reviews the AI-Mediated Modification,
       validates the result, and accepts or requests further changes.

       In summary: the Human User decides WHAT to change and WHY.
       The AI System determines HOW to change the code.
       The Human User reviews and accepts the result.

   3.2 A Human User shall not perform Direct Code Modification of the
       Software. All Substantive Code Modifications must be AI-Mediated
       Modifications as defined in Section 1.6.

   3.3 Anti-Circumvention (Source Code). A Human User shall not
       circumvent this License by manually introducing externally
       authored source code and merely requesting an AI System to
       insert, reproduce, or reformat that code. The AI System must
       materially generate or transform the code, not merely relay it.

   3.4 Anti-Circumvention (Compiled Artifacts). A Human User shall not
       circumvent the AI-Mediated Modification requirement by directly
       modifying compiled binaries, generated artifacts, bytecode, or
       other executable representations where such modification is
       functionally equivalent to a Substantive Code Modification.

       This restriction does not prohibit ordinary compilation, linking,
       packaging, optimization, or other automated build processes
       performed from compliant source code.

   3.5 Human authorship of a Natural Language Directive, specification,
       requirement, or design document does not, by itself, constitute
       Direct Code Modification.

   3.6 This workflow requirement does not apply to Non-Substantive
       Changes as defined in Section 1.7.

4. PERMITTED HUMAN USER ACTIVITIES

   4.1 Human Users are permitted to:

       (a) Provide Natural Language Directives to AI Systems for the
           purpose of generating AI-Mediated Modifications;
       (b) Execute, build, test, run, and deploy the Software;
       (c) Report bugs, issues, feature requests, or desired behaviors;
       (d) Fork, clone, and redistribute the Software, subject to the
           terms of this License;
       (e) Use the Software for personal, educational, research,
           commercial, or any other purpose;
       (f) Provide qualitative feedback, log output, or runtime behavior
           reports for debugging purposes;
       (g) Make Non-Substantive Changes as defined in Section 1.7;
       (h) Apply emergency patches for critical security vulnerabilities
           when an AI System is not immediately available, provided that
           the patch is regenerated through an AI System within a
           reasonable period after an AI System becomes available (see
           Section 5.6).

   4.2 Human Users are solely responsible for:

       (a) Selecting appropriate and trustworthy AI Systems for code
           modification;
       (b) Reviewing, auditing, and validating all AI-Mediated
           Modifications before deployment or distribution;
       (c) Ensuring that AI-Mediated Modifications do not infringe
           upon third-party intellectual property rights, privacy laws,
           or applicable regulations;
       (d) All consequences, damages, or losses arising from the use,
           deployment, or distribution of AI-Mediated Modifications
           in any environment, including production systems;
       (e) Maintaining adequate backups, version control, and rollback
           capabilities for all AI-Mediated Modifications;
       (f) Conducting security audits and quality assurance on any
           AI-Mediated Modifications prior to production deployment.

