   5.1 AI may generate the code.
       AI does not assume legal responsibility for the code.
       The Human User assumes all responsibility.

   5.2 THE HUMAN USER ACKNOWLEDGES AND AGREES that they bear sole and
       complete responsibility for the use, modification, and
       distribution of the Software and any AI-Mediated Modifications
       thereof. The Author shall not be held liable for any damages,
       defects, security vulnerabilities, data loss, system failures,
       business interruption, or any other consequences resulting from
       the use or modification of the Software.

   5.3 THE HUMAN USER acknowledges that AI Systems may produce code
       containing errors, security flaws, unintended behavior,
       hallucinated implementations, outdated dependencies, or
       non-terminating execution paths. The Human User is responsible
       for thoroughly reviewing, testing, and validating all
       AI-Mediated Modifications prior to use in any environment,
       especially production or safety-critical systems.

   5.4 THE HUMAN USER shall be responsible for, and shall not hold the
       Author liable for, any claims, damages, losses, liabilities,
       costs, and expenses arising from or relating to the Human User's
       use, modification, or redistribution of the Software, including
       but not limited to AI-Mediated Modifications.

   5.5 No warranty is made that AI-Mediated Modifications will be
       accurate, complete, secure, performant, or free of defects. The
       Human User must perform independent verification, code review,
       and quality assurance appropriate to their specific use case and
       risk tolerance.

   5.6 Emergency Exception. In the event of a critical security
       vulnerability or catastrophic bug where an AI System is not
       immediately available, a Human User may apply a temporary direct
       patch. However, the Human User must regenerate the patch through
       an AI System within a reasonable period after an AI System
       becomes available for use, and must document the emergency
       modification. Failure to do so may be considered a license
       violation.

6. AI MODIFICATION RECORD (Recommended)

   6.1 This Section is a recommendation, not a requirement. Compliance
       with this License does not depend on maintaining an AI
       Modification Record.

   6.2 The Author recommends that projects using this License maintain
       an AI Modification Record to document the provenance of changes.
       A suggested format is:

       .aiopl/
           modifications/
               2026-09-02-001.json

       {
           "license": "AI-OPL-1.2",
           "agent": "Claude Code",
           "files": ["src/main.py", "src/utils.py"],
           "human_directive": "Refactor the parser and add error handling",
           "timestamp": "2026-09-02T22:40:00+09:00"
       }

       The record MAY omit or redact confidential, personal,
       security-sensitive, or proprietary information.

   6.3 The Author further recommends that commits containing AI-Mediated
       Modifications include a trailer such as:

       Co-authored-by: <AI System Name>

       or a similar marker to indicate AI involvement in the change.

   6.4 These records are advisory only and do not create legal
       obligations. They exist to support transparency and to help
       establish a culture of AI-aware development practices.

